## 🛡️ 3. Architecture Seams & Invariants

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    subgraph CoreDomain ["Core Domain (Invariants & Rules)"]
        A["Domain Models / State Machine"]
    end

    subgraph ServiceLayer ["Service & Coordination Layer"]
        B["Highest Testing Seam (Coordinator / Engine)"]
    end

    subgraph Adapters ["External Adapters (I/O, CLI, Storage, Web)"]
        C["External Clients / Drivers"]
    end

    C --> B
    B --> A
```

- **Domain Invariants**: States and invariants that must hold under all concurrency and error conditions.
- **Highest Testing Seam**: Primary behavioral verification boundary (test whole workflows through this seam with zero brittle private mocks).

